  "blocks": {
    "\"Configure the harness to use the Linear MCP server — it exposes the Linear API as tools the agent can call. Saves you writing custom tool wrappers.\"": "“配置运行框架使用 Linear MCP 服务器——它会把 Linear API 暴露成智能体可调用的工具，省去编写自定义工具包装器的工作。”",
    "\"The agent needs to read tickets from Linear.\"": "“智能体需要从 Linear 读取任务。”",
    "Many harnesses now mitigate this with tool search: instead of the full definitions, the context holds a context pointer to the available tools — the agent searches for a tool by name or purpose and loads its definition only when it needs it. If your harness doesn't do this, the up-front cost still applies, and it's worth enabling only the servers a project actually needs.": "许多运行框架现在通过工具搜索缓解这个问题：上下文不再保存完整定义，而只保存指向可用工具的<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context-pointer\">上下文指针</a>；智能体按名称或用途搜索工具，只在需要时加载定义。如果你的运行框架没有这样做，前置成本仍然存在，因此只应启用项目真正需要的服务器。",
    "Model Context Protocol. A protocol for plugging external tool servers into a harness — how an agent gets tools beyond what the harness ships with. The agent never \"calls MCP\"; it calls a tool, and the harness happens to have gotten that tool from an MCP server. Also exposes resources (read-only data) and prompts (reusable templates), but tool provision is the primary use.": "MCP 即模型上下文协议（Model Context Protocol），是一种把外部工具服务器接入<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/harness\">运行框架</a>的协议，让<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agent\">智能体</a>获得框架内置能力以外的<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/tool\">工具</a>。智能体从不会“调用 MCP”；它调用的是工具，只不过这个工具恰好由运行框架从 MCP 服务器获取。MCP 还可以暴露资源（只读数据）和提示词（可复用模板），但提供工具是最主要的用途。",
    "The cost is paid in context. Every tool a server advertises arrives as a definition — name, description, parameter schema — and the model can only call tools it knows about. The naive approach loads every definition into the context window up front: install a few generous servers and a session starts with thousands of tokens of tool schemas before you've typed anything, spending attention budget on tools the task will never use.": "代价由<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context\">上下文</a>承担。服务器声明的每个工具都会以定义形式进入其中——名称、描述和参数 schema——而<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/model\">模型</a>只能调用自己知道的工具。最直接的做法是预先把所有定义加载进<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context-window\">上下文窗口</a>：只需安装几个功能丰富的服务器，<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/session\">会话</a>就可能在你输入任何内容前，先装入数千个 <a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/token\">Token</a> 的工具 schema，把<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/attention-budget\">注意力预算</a>花在任务永远不会使用的工具上。",
    "The protocol solves an integration problem. Without a standard, every harness would need its own Linear integration, its own Slack integration, its own database integration — written and maintained separately for each. With MCP, the integration is written once as a server, and any MCP-compatible harness can use it. The harness connects to the server, the server advertises what tools it offers, and those tools become available to the agent alongside the built-in ones.": "该协议解决的是集成问题。如果没有标准，每个运行框架都需要分别编写和维护自己的 Linear 集成、Slack 集成和数据库集成。有了 MCP，一项集成只需作为服务器编写一次，任何兼容 MCP 的运行框架都能使用。运行框架连接服务器，服务器声明自己提供哪些工具，这些工具随后会与内置工具一起供智能体使用。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>"
